#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:5 43f84ca4b6c24f67a522c3a6373f08c7
msgid "Archived: Installing the PX4FMU on a QuadCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:9 5b9f8b15d40143bd9d7f25d9016e1ea5
msgid "**ARCHIVED ARTICLE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:11 b42da4b2939c4727823341ca80a3a861
msgid ""
"This article is for creating a quadcopter using the PX4FMU only, which is"
" one approach for creating a very small autopilot. `Arsovtech "
"<http://arsovtech.com/?p=1447>`__ have created a small Pixhawk based "
"board that is much more popular with the community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:17 a773b94ec8b84df0b0001a2e5f7a0047
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:19 38b62d15ac284bf88b3628ce11e8cd63
msgid "**Bill Of Materials:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:21 6e0c9dacb5424cb88a1dc18024afdfb7
msgid ""
"Copter firmware version 3.1 and later supports only the combined system "
"of the PX4 FMU and PX4 IO board; the FMU-only system is no longer "
"supported. Purchase a PX4 FMU kit from 3DRobotics LINK_BROKEN and a PX4 "
"I/O board LINK_BROKEN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:25 c034a8bce67c43f5bacf3e5c70db7f07
msgid ""
"A special cable that fits into the PX4's main \"Multi\" connector will "
"allow you to perform the primary wiring and it is available from "
"3DRobotics LINK_BROKEN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:28 8384471c808947a9bb0ed6c225c487c8
msgid ""
"If you choose, you can cut off the single pin connectors and solder "
"directly to the necessary locations and trim back the excess wires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:30 a1462cb100294bc5aef500293a8838c1
msgid ""
"Use the 4 supplied nylon standoffs to mount the PX4FMU to a piece of "
"scrap plastic or fiberglass sheet the same size as the FMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:33 424d2c778c864b518e0efa04ed1b7e26
msgid ""
"Mount the board to your copter with four 3/4\" squares of Kyosho Zeal gel"
" or double sided foam tape to provide vibration isolation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:36 be33732053f04b14a212f071ac8c8617
msgid ""
"**Mount your PX4-FMU board in a central location on top of your "
"QuadCopter.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:39 fe9ec012611541ee877984ff279f9ef5
msgid "The PX4FMU board Normally has the SD card on top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:40 f24e40cf045f48b18d8a67ecda275620
msgid ""
"It can sometimes be advantageous to mount the PX4FMU with the other side "
"up for better LED observation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:42 987e3b2023c3499ebf3be00b979b0b1f
msgid ""
"If you do mount the PX4FMU board with the Component side up it will be "
"necessary to set the \"Board Orientation (AHRS_ORIENTATION)\" parameter "
"to \"Roll 180\" in the Advanced Parameter List in Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:46 c66524481eaa4b77ad434494bf606e18
msgid ""
"The arrow labeled \"FRONT\" should be facing to the front of the aircraft"
" (also the large black board interconnect connector)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:48 ce4de08f25f74bb5a3e6d0f0904b016c
msgid ""
"If you use the vibration dampers suggested above it is best to put a "
"small O-ring on top of the damper and under the PX4 Board before "
"fastening it \"gently\" down with the supplied nuts to prevent damage to "
"the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:52 d0c0809bde81450d873ab93d80f114b5
msgid ""
"In fact, these dampers may not provide adequate damping and you should "
"review the Wiki section on vibration control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:55 9a585b5149834964919ca61ccb191337
msgid "**Mount the GPS facing up with an unobstructed \"view\" of the sky**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:57 152d79bb76ff4004be7b92cc6461fba5
msgid ""
"The GPS can be mounted on a short riser to give it the widest satellite "
"access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:61 f77151a031504c4fa37a739a376bd74e
msgid "PX4-FMU Only Wiring Diagram for QuadCopters using a PPM-SUM receiver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:67 d5ed5abf52f04842af79cdced003f6b9
msgid "Wiring the PX4FMU Board to Your QuadCopter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:69 4ad869636e764c468d33202ff063bb66
msgid ""
"**Use heavy gauge wire to interconnect the ESC's Ground and power leads "
"to a Battery Connector.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:72 e41724b1c502432e9559f13d2f20120c
msgid "A Power Distribution board can also be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:74 0cddebc5b6a741b58fb70dbc673f2f9e
msgid ""
"**Connect your BEC (5 volt power supply) power in leads to the battery "
"input leads.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:78 06834dbdda3949da9636f971b1592ab2
msgid ""
"Connect the BEC Ground output to the PX4's Ground (Multi connector pin "
"15)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:80 cda52c7b895548f09cb96d601cc1c4b7
msgid ""
"Connect the BEC Power output to the PX4's power In (Multi connector pin "
"1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:82 690e487fee03495594fa0948373cd143
msgid ""
"**NOTE!** Instead of a separate BEC as shown, the power and ground leads "
"(signal side) from one of your ESCs that contains a BEC can be wired to "
"the Multi connectors pins 1 and 15 to provide PX4 board power."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:87 17d290cbf21549eb9cfffdd8636df85b
msgid ""
"**The PPM-SUM receiver may be wired with a connecting cable as shown in "
"the diagram above.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:90 7b2ad2cdee5340e68211f29871e46391
msgid ""
"Or the PPM-SUM signal and power and ground leads from the 15 pin DF13 "
"\"Multi\" connector may be directly wired to a 3 pin servo/receiver "
"connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:93 2c87f6c7472f472eafc07f848828afd4
msgid ""
"Connect your PPM-Sum RC receivers signal wire to pin 6 of the Multi "
"connector on the PX4 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:95 dbe5f6dd6c8445d393bbe7609fca93ae
msgid ""
"Connect the PPM-SUM RC Receivers Ground lead to pin 15 of the Multi "
"connector on the PX4 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:97 65700a70f5d84eb4ac246c4cd3c5d510
msgid ""
"Connect the PPM-SUM RC Receivers Power lead to pin 1 of the Multi "
"connector on the PX4 board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:100
#: 68d3b8f8a7834398a8ffe05d0d7038df
msgid "**Wire the PX4FMU board's 4 servo out signals to the ESC control inputs.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:103
#: 4cba4f42b88043c3944dd994f89dd5cc
msgid ""
"The wires can be put together with connectors as shown in the diagram or "
"solder and heat shrink tubing can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:105
#: ebcb978c394a44308d6bec7a4a811371
msgid ""
"Wire PX4FMU PWM control 4 (Multi Connector pin 9) to The ESC signal in "
"for Motor 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:107
#: 58a18b6b40f04fd396a264fe57b6d67b
msgid ""
"Wire PX4FMU PWM control 2 (Multi Connector pin 10) to The ESC signal in "
"for Motor 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:109
#: b320fc705d09466d95df9a7098eae74e
msgid ""
"Wire PX4FMU PWM control 1 (Multi Connector pin 11) to The ESC signal in "
"for Motor 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:111
#: f393d25460cf4817a99cfd0ddbe8072a
msgid ""
"Wire PX4FMU PWM control 3 (Multi Connector pin 12) to The ESC signal in "
"for Motor 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:114
#: 68685b3e600341158ca6b7494dc9301b
msgid ""
"**Run a wire from the PX4FMU's Battery Monitor connection (Multi "
"Connector pin 5) to the positive battery power lead.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:116
#: 1ddf810bc7e546138fdfb7a1c6f5d6b1
msgid ""
"**Note! The cable that is supplied in the plastic envelope with the UBLOX"
" GPS which has white 6 pin connectors on both ends is NOT the correct "
"cable for the PX4**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:120
#: f3cf86eb221f4f33b77bb909a7a0fcb6
msgid ""
"The correct longer cable is provided in a separate envelope and has a 5 "
"pin \"beige\" connector on one end and a 6 pin white connector on the "
"other end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:123
#: 4b5f4c5861d74a9ca66d3f6893a3eac9
msgid ""
"Plug the correct GPS cable's white 6 pin connector into the 6 pin socket "
"on the GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:125
#: 9fa66409a99246119c9f2a2313a29c50
msgid ""
"Plug the beige 5 pin connector into the PX4's 5 pin GPS socket which is "
"next to the 15 pin DF13 Mini connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:128
#: 02eeb74b9597485cbfbd37e3cce5646a
msgid ""
"**Plug the 2 pin connector attached to the lead supplied with the buzzer "
"into the buzzer socket on the side of the PX4FMU board that has the SD "
"card holder on it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:131
#: 59a62c7b8f154db6b02a0d5e52f0cd09
msgid ""
"In Mission Planner in the Complete Parameter List it will be necessary "
"for you to set the **BRD_SAFETYENABLE** parameter to 0 = off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/px4fmu-only-wiring.rst:135
#: 6cad17d3fc3a4b068c0a0f40d5df4b0b
msgid ""
"This is because the safety switch connects to the IO board's on board "
"microcontroller and there is no switch for the PX4FMU only."
msgstr ""

